## Performance Budget

| Operation | Budget | Approach |
|-----------|--------|----------|
| Parse viewport (80×24) | <10ms | Read 1920 cells, group, classify |
| Parse viewport (200×50) | <30ms | Larger viewports, same algorithm |
| Full scrollback reparse | <100ms | Only on resize, not per-frame |
| React render (20 blocks) | <16ms | Virtual list, memo'd components |
| Memory per cached block | <1KB | Line refs, not copied text |
| WebSocket throughput | Unaffected | Data goes to hidden xterm, React reads buffer |

### Optimization Strategies

1. **Incremental parsing** — On new output, only re-parse lines from the last known block boundary to the cursor, not the entire viewport.
2. **Block caching** — Cache classified blocks by row range. Invalidate only when those rows change.
3. **Virtual scrolling** — Only render blocks visible in the viewport. Use intersection observer or fixed-height estimation for off-screen blocks.
4. **Debounced re-render** — Batch multiple xterm writes into a single React render cycle.

